    <briefdescription>
<para>Optional capability of a <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_hypo_elastic" kindref="compound">MaterialHypoElastic</ref>: a stress update that also yields the energy tangents. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A material provides the derivatives of its updated elastic energy density and dissipation wrt the strain increment by inheriting from this class next to <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_hypo_elastic" kindref="compound">MaterialHypoElastic</ref>. Elements find the capability with <computeroutput>dynamic_cast&lt; const HypoElasticEnergyTangentProvider* &gt;( material )</computeroutput> and call this variant instead of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_materials_1_1_material_hypo_elastic_1af7065b0795b68e6010b1e313ee962b7e" kindref="member">MaterialHypoElastic::computeStress</ref> only when they assemble energy gradients, e.g., for dissipation based arc length control. The standard material interface is not affected. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
